W: Timmer stairs fears me,
W: I thought it wrong to lie my lane
W: When I'm sae near my deary.
W:
W: 2. O had your apron bidden doon,
W: The kirk wad ne'er hae kend it,
W: But since the word's gane through the toon,
W: My dear, I canna mend it.  [Chorus]
W:
W: 3. But ye maun mount the cutty-stool
W: And I maun mount the pillar,
W: And that's the way the poor folks dae,
W: Because they hae nae siller.  [Chorus]
%
