W: 1. Avenging and bright fall the swift sword of Erin.
W: On him who the brave sons of Usna betrayed.
W: For ev'ry fond eye which he wakened a tear in,
W: A drop from his heartwounds shall weep o'er her blade.
W:
W: 2. By the red cloud that hung over Conor's dark dwelling,
W: When Ulad's three champions lay sleeping in gore.
W: By the billows of war which so often high swelling
W: Have wafted these heroes to victory's shore.
W:
W: 3. We swear to revenge them! No joy shall be tasted,
W: The harp shall be silent, the maiden unwed,
W: Our halls shall be mute, and our field shall lie wasted,
W: 'Till vengeance is wreck'd on the murderer's head!
W:
W: 4. Yes, monarch! tho' sweet are our home recollections,
W: Tho' sweet are the tears that from tenderness fall;
W: Tho' sweet are our friendships, our hopes and affections,
W: Revenge on a tyrant is sweetest of all!
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_c273ed90.abc

