W:2. Three short steps, I stepped up to her
W:Not knowing her as she passed me by
W:I stepped up to her, thinking for to view her
W:She appeared to be like some virtuous bride
W:
W:3. I says "Fair maid, where are you going?
W:And what's the occasion of all your grief?
W:I will make you as happy as any lady
W:If you will grant to me one small relief"
W:
W:4. "Stand off, stand off, you're a false deceiver
W:You are a false deceitful man, I know
W:'Tis you that has caused my poor heart to wander
W:And in your comfort lies no refrain"
W:
W:5. So I'll go down to some lonesome valley
W:Where no man on earth shall there me find
W:Where the pretty little small birds do change their voices
W:And every moment blows blusterous wind
W:
W:6. So come all young men who go a-sailing
W:Pray pay attention to what I say
W:For there's many a dark and a cloudy morning
W:Turns out to be a sun shiny day
