%
W: 1. Come all ye young fellows who follow the sea,
W: To me! Wey-hey, blow the man down!
W: And pray pay attention and listen to me.
W: Give me some time to blow the man down!
W:
W: 2. I'm a deep water sailor just in from Hong Kong,
W: To me! Wey-hey, blow the man down!
W: You buy me a drink, and I'll sing you this song.
W: Give me some time to blow the man down!
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Blow the man down, bullies, blow the man down,
W: Wey-hey, blow the man down!
W: Blow him right back into Liverpool town,
W: Give me some time to blow the man down!
W:
W: 3. There's tinkers and tailors and soldiers and all,
W: To me! Wey-hey, blow the man down!
W: They all ship for sailors on board the Black Ball.
W: Give me some time to blow the man down!
W:
W: 4. You'll see those poor devils how they will all scoot,
W: Wey-hey, blow the man down!
W: Aisted along by the toe of a boot.
W: Give me some time to blow the man down!
W:
W: 5. It's starboard and larboard on deck they will sprawl,
W: To me! Wey-hey, blow the man down!
W: For kickin' Jack Williams commands the Black Ball.
W: Give me some time to blow the man down!
W:
W: 6. Lay aft now, ya lubbers, lay aft now I say,
W: To me! Wey-hey, blow the man down!
W: I'll none of yer dodges on my ship today.
W: Give me some time to blow the man down!
W:
W: 7. So I'll give you fair warning before we belay,
W: To me! Wey-hey, blow the man down!
W: Don't ever take heed of what chantymen say.
W: Give me some time to blow the man down!
