W: 1. Hie upon hielands and laigh upon Tay,
W: Bonnie George Campbell rode out on a day.
W: He saddled, he bridled, and gallant rode he
W: Oh, hame cam his guid horse, but never cam he.
W:
W: 2. Out cam his mother, dear, greeting fu sair
W: And out cam his bonnie bryde riving her hair.
W: The meadow lies green, the corn is unshorn,
W: But bonnie George Campbell will never return.
W:
W: 3. Saddled and bridled and booted rode he,
W: A plume in his helmet, a sword at his knee,
W: But toom* cam his saddle all bloody to see,
W: Oh, hame cam his guid horse, but never cam he.
W:
W:
W: *Note: "toom" means "empty"
