W: 1. On Halloween night you’d better flee
W: From a creature known as “Mister B.”
W: He’s a monster of malignancy,
W: He’ll catch you if you’re slow. (Hunnh!)
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Soon will the Boogeyman come,
W: He’ll scare you silly and strike you dumb,
W: When Halloween is over and done,
W: He’ll eat your brain and go.
W:
W: 2. Formed from mist and graveyard fog,
W: Eye of newt and hair of dog,
W: He’ll rise up from his dismal bog,
W: And catch you if you’re slow. (Hunnh!)
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 3. Formed from muck and graveyard clay,
W: He hunts by night and spooks by day,
W: Run and try to get away,
W: He’ll catch you if you’re slow. (Hunnh!)
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. Born of muck and graveyard mold,
W: His eyes are blank, his touch is cold,
W: He’ll put you in a stranglehold
W: And eat your brains and go! (Hunnh!)
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 5. On Halloween night you’d better flee
W: Beware, beware of “Mister B,”
W: He’s a dumpster of depravity,
W: He’ll catch you if you’re slow. (Hunnh!)
W: (Chorus - Repeat last two lines)
%
