%
W: 1. Oh Bridget O'Malley, you have left my heart shaken,
W: With a hopeless desolation I'd have you to know.
W: It's the wonders of admiration your quiet face has taken
W: And your beauty will haunt me wherever I go.
W:
W: 2. The white moon above the pale sands, the pale stars above the thorn tree
W: Are cold beside my darling, but no purer than she.
W: I gaze upon the cold moon till the stars drown in the warm seas
W: But the bright eyes of my darling are never on me.
W:
W: 3. My Sunday is weary, my Sunday it is grey now,
W: My heart is a cold thing, my heart is a stone.
W: All joy is dead in me, my life has gone away now
W: For some other has taken my love for his own.
W:
W: 4. The day it is approaching when we were to be married
W: But it's rather I would die than live only to grieve.
W: Oh, meet me, my darling, e'er the sun sets o'er the barley,
W: I'll wait for you there on the road to Drumslieve.
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_1f9b3936.abc

