"D" D2 FE"G" D2 D2 |"D" D6 z2 |]
w: ven- tur- ing your sweet|lives.|
%
%%wordsspace 18
%
W: 1. Come all you married seamen bold a few lines to you I'll write,
W: Just to let you know how the game do go when you are out of sight,
W: Just to let you know how the lads on shore go sporting with your wives,
W: While you are on the rolling seas and venturing your sweet lives.
W:
W: 2. It's now our ship she's outward bound and ready for to sail,
W: May the Heavens above protect my love with a sweet and pleasant gale,
W: And keep him clear all from the shore and never more return,
W: Until his pockets are well lined and then he's welcome home.
W:
W: 3. A last farewell she takes of him and she begins to cry,
W: A-taking out her handkerchief to wipe her weeping eyes,
W: My husband's gone to sea, she cries, how hard it is my case,
W: But still on shore there's plenty more, another will take his place.
W:
W: 4. Then she goes unto her fancy man these words to him did say,
W: My husband he is gone to sea, tomorrow is half-pay day,
W: And you must wait at the dockyard gate until that I come out,
W: For that very day we'll sweat his half-pay and drink both ale and stout.
W:
W: 5. That day they spent in sweet content till the half-pay was no more,
W: Then, never mind, my dear, she cries, he's working hard for more,
W: Perhaps he's at the masthead a-dying with the cold,
W: Or perhaps he's at his watch on deck, our joys he can't behold.
W:
W: 6. And now our ship she's homeward bound brought up in Plymouth Sound,
W: She hears the gun, My husband's come, to him I must go down,
W: She goes unto her neighbour's house, One thing of you I crave,
W: Lend me your gown for mine's in pawn, It's the only one I have.
W:
W: 7. Then she goes down unto the Sound and tries for to get in,
W: She so loudly for her husband calls and runs and kisses him,
W: Saying, How happy we shall be, my dear, now you are safe on shore,
W: You shall sit at home with me, my love, and go to sea no more.
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_8e6089d7.abc

