K:Em
%
B, | "Em" E2 F G2 F | "D" EDE "Em" B,3 | G2 F GGA | "G" B3 "D" A z G/A/ |
w: There was a la-dy lived_ in York, All a-lone-y, a-lone-y, She_
"Em" B2 B "D" AGF | "C" GFE "Bm" B,3 | "Em" EEEB,2 A, | "Bm" B,2 E "Em" E2 z |]
w: She fell in love with her fa-ther's clerk, Down by the green-wood side_y.
%
W: 1. There was a lady lived in York,
W: All aloney, aloney,
W: She fell in love with her father's clerk,
W: Down by the greenwood sidey.
W:
W: 2. He courted her a year and a day,
W: All aloney, aloney
W: And then he did that girl betray.
W: Down by the greenwood sidey.
W:
W: 3. She leaned her back against a thorn,
W: And there she had two pretty babes born.
W:
W: 4. She had a penknife long and sharp.
W: She pierced those tender babies' hearts.
W:
W: 5. She washed the knife clean in the flood,
W: She turned the river all to blood.
W:
W: 6. She buried them under a marble stone,
W: And then she turned her face toward home.
W:
W: 7. As she came by her father's hall,
W: She saw two pretty babes playing at ball.
W:
W: 8. "Oh babes! Oh babes! If you were mine,"
W: "I'd dress you up in silks so fine."
W:
W: 9. "Oh mother! Oh mother! We once were thine,"
W: "You did not prove to us so kind."
W:
W: 10. "Seven years, seven years you shall burn in Hell,"
W: "Seven years and you won't see heaven until.”
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_fa48d53b.abc

