X:71
T:The False Knight on the Road
M:4/4
L:1/8
K:D
%
"D" dBAF AAAB|d2de fefe|dBAF A2AB|d2de fdd2|
w: "Whe-re are you go-ing?" said the false knight_ on the road. "I'm go-ing to the school," said the wee boy and still he stood.
fefg a2gf| "Em" e2b2 befe| "D" dBAF A2AB|d2de fdd2|]
w: "What is on your back?" says the false knight on the road. "Me bun-dles and me books," said the wee boy and still he stood.
%
%leftmargin 1.5in
%
W: 2. "I came a-walking by your home," said the false knight on the road.
W: "It lay in your way," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W: "Flung your dog a stone," said the false knight on the road,
W: "I wish it was a bone," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W:
W: 3. "What sheep and cattle's that?", said the false knight on the road.
W: "They're mine and me father's," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W: "How many shall be mine?" said the false knight on the road,
W: "The ones that have blue tails," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W:
W: 4. "I wish you were in yonder tree," said the false knight on the road.
W: "A ladder under me," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W: "Ladder it will break." said the false knight on the road,
W: "And you will surely fall," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W:
W: 5. "I wish you were in yonder sea," said the false knight on the road.
W: "A good boat under me," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W: "The boat will surely sink," said the false knight on the road,
W: "Then you will surely drown," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W:
W: 6. "Has your mother more than you?" said the false knight on the road.
W: "And none of them for you," said the wee boy and still he stood.
W: "Think I hear a bell," said the false knight on the road.
W: "It's ringing you to Hell," said the wee boy and still he stood.
%
