W: 1. The sun was setting in the west
W: The birds were singing on ev'ry tree
W: All nature seemed inclined to rest
W: But still there was no rest for me.
W:
W: [Chorus:]
W: Farewell to Nova Scotia, the sea-bound coast
W: Let your mountains dark and dreary be
W: And when I am far away on the briny oceans tossed
W: Will you ever heave a sigh and a wish for me?
W:
W: 2. I grieve to leave my native land
W: I grieve to leave my comrades all
W: And my aged parents whom I always held so dear
W: And the bonnie, bonnie lass that I do adore.
W: [Chorus]
W:
W: 3. The drums they do beat and the wars do alarm
W: The captain calls, we must obey
W: So farewell, farewell to Nova Scotia's charms
W: For it's early in the morning I am far, far away.
W: [Chorus]
W:
W: 4. I have three brothers and they are at rest
W: Their arms are folded on their breast
W: But a poor simple sailor just like me
W: Must be tossed and driven on the dark blue sea.
W: [Chorus]
%
