%
%lyrics:  http://mysongbook.de/msb/songs/e/emigrant.html
%
W: 1. Farewell to old Ireland the land of my childhood
W: That now and forever I am bound for to leave
W: Farewell to the shores where the shamrock is growing
W: It's the bright spot of beauty in the home of the brave
W: I will think on its valleys with fond admiration
W: Though never again its green hills will I see
W: For I'm bound for to cross o'er the wild swelling ocean
W: In search of fame fortune and sweet liberty
W:
W: 2. It's hard to be forced from the lands that we live in
W: Our houses and farms we're obliged for to sell
W: And to wander alone among Indians and strangers
W: To Find some sweet spot where our children may dwell
W: O I have a wee lassie I fain would take with me
W: Her dwelling at present lies in County Down
W: It would break my poor heart for to leave her behind me
W: We'll both roam together this wide world around
W:
W: 3. So it's come along Bessie my own blue-eyed lassie
W: Bid farewell to your mother and then come with me
W: And I'll make my endeavour for to keep your mind easy
W: Till we reach the green fields of Amerikay
W: Our ship at the present lies in lovely Derry
W: To bear us away o'er the wild swelling sea
W: May heaven be her pilot and grant her fond breezes
W: Till we reach the green fields of Amerikay
W:
W: 4. Our artists our farmers our tradesmen are leaving
W: To seek for employment far over the sea
W: Where they will get riches with care and with industry
W: There is nothing but hardship at home if you spin
W: So it's cheer up your hearts now you lads and gay lassies
W: There's gold for the digging and lots of it too
W: Here's health to the heart that has courage to venture
W: Bad luck to the lad or the lass that would rue
W:
W: 5. There's brandy in Quebec at ten cents a quart boys
W: The ale in New Brunswick's a penny a glass
W: There is wine in that sweet town they call Montreal boys
W: At inn after inn we will drink as we pass
W: And we'll call for a bumper of ale wine and brandy
W: And we'll drink to the health of those far far away
W: Our hearts will all warm at the thoughts of old Ireland
W: When we're in the green fields of Amerikay
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_8836e542.abc

