W: 1. Just sit right back and you'll hear a tale,
W: To make your trotters shake,
W: Of several starving castaways,
W: And their lunch at Gilligan's wake,
W: Their lunch at Gilligan's Wake.
W:
W: 2. An earthquake shook bold Gilligan's isle,
W: With tidal waves galore,
W: Their food supply was washed away,
W: And they could not get no more,
W: They could not get no more.
W:
W: 3. "Now, listen here!" the skipper said,
W: "We're perishing by degrees,
W: It's surely time - it ain't no crime,
W: To invoke the law of the seas,
W: The terrible law of the seas."
W:
W: 4. "Old skippers in the days of yore,
W: Oft did this rule employ,
W: In cases of starvation,
W: Just eat the cabin boy,
W: Just eat the cabin boy."
W:
W: 5. "The 'Minnow' being very small,
W: We'd hardly any crew,
W: And since we have no cabin boy,
W: Our Gilligan will do,
W: Our Gilligan will do."
W:
W: 6. "Goodbye Little Buddy," the skipper said,
W: "It grieves my heart full sore,
W: It’s not that I love you any the less,
W: But I love protein more,
W: Yes I love protein more."
W:
W: 7. So they held a wake for Gilligan's sake,
W: They buried his shoes and shirt.
W: The buryin' being hungry work,
W: They had Ginger for dessert,
W: They had Ginger for dessert.
