W: 1. If you'd seen my dearest, his eyes shined the clearest.
W: His lips like the red blood that's new dropped in snow.
W: He was neat, tall and slender, his eyes soft and tender.
W: He'll be my greenwood laddie where ever I go.
W:
W: 2. My parents, my darling, they slight you and they scorn you
W: Because you've no riches all wrapped up in store.
W: But the more that they slight you, the more I'll invite you
W: To be my greenwood laddie and boy I adore
W:
W: 3. But if I had the wealth of the East and West Indies,
W: If I had the gold on the African Shore,
W: Or if I could gain thousands, I'd lie on your bosom.
W: You'd be my Greenwood Laddie and the boy I adore.
W:
W: 4. It's down in yon bower we spent many the long hour
W: A plucking the red rose by yon clear winding shore.
W: It was his stolen kisses caused my fondest wishes.
W: He'll be my greenwood laddie til time is no more.
W:
W: 5. If you'd seen my dearest, his eyes shined the clearest.
W: His lips like the red blood so new dropped in snow.
W: He was neat, tall and slender, his eyes soft and tender.
W: He'll be my greenwood laddie til time is no more.
