W:1. Here we come a wassailing among the leaves so green,
W:Here we come a wandering so fair to be seen.
W:
W:(Refrain:)
W:Love and joy come to you and to your wassail too
W:And God bless you and send you a happy New Year
W:And God send you a happy New Year.
W:
W:2. We are not daily beggars that beg from door to door,
W:We are your neighbor's children whom you have seen before.
W:(Refrain:)
W:
W:3. We have got a little purse of stretching leather skin;
W:We want a little money to line it well within.
W:(Refrain:)
W:
W:4. God bless the master of this house, likewise the mistress, too,
W:And all the little children that round the table go.
W:(Refrain:)
W:
W:5. Good Master and good Mistress, while you sit by the fire,
W:Pray think of us poor children a-wandering in the mire.
W:(Refrain:)
