W: 1. The host is riding from Knocknarea
W: And over the grave of Clooth-na-Bare;
W: Caoilte tossing his burning hair
W: And Niamh calling Away, come away.
W:
W: 2. Empty your mind of its mortal dream.
W: The winds awaken, the leaves whirl round,
W: Our cheeks are pale, our hair is unbound,
W: Our breasts are heaving, our eyes are agleam.
W:
W: 3. Our arms are waving, our lips are apart;
W: And if any gaze on our rushing band,
W: We come between him and the deed of his hand,
W: We come between him and the hope of his heart
W:
W: 4. The host is rushing twixt night and day,
W: And where is there hope or deed as fair?
W: Caoilte tossing his burning hair,
W: and Niamh calling Away, come away
