W: Chorus:
W: I never will marry,
W: I'll be no man's wife.
W: I intend to live single
W: All the days of my life.
W:
W: 1. Some say that love is a gentle thing,
W: It only has brought me pain,
W: And the only boy I ever loved
W: Is gone on that midnight train.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 2. Your company, your company,
W: Your company unto me,
W: It makes me feel while I'm away,
W: That every day is three.
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 3. You'll see the grass whereon you stand,
W: Arise and grow again,
W: But love it is a killin’ thing.
W: Did you ever feel the pain?
W: (Chorus)
W:
W: 4. I wish my heart were made of glass,
W: Wherein you might behold,
W: All the wonders of my love,
W: The letters are writ in gold.
W: (Chorus)
%
