W: 1. Sportsmen arouse, the morning is clear
W: The larks are singing all in the air
W: Sportsmen arouse, the morning is clear
W: The larks are singing all in the air
W: Go tell your sweet lover, the hounds are out
W: Go tell your sweet lover the hounds are out
W: Saddle your horses, your saddles prepare
W: We'll away to cover to seek for a hare.
W:
W: 2. We searched the woods the groves all around
W: The trail being over, the game being found...
W: We searched the woods the groves all around
W: The trail being over, the game being found...
W: Then u-up she springs, through brake she flies...
W: Then u-up she springs, through brake she flies...
W: Follow, follow the musical horn
W: Sing follow, hark follow, the innocent hare.
W:
W: 3. The huntsman blows his joyful sound
W: Tally ho, me boys, all over the down
W: The huntsman blows his joyful sound
W: Tally ho, me boys, all over the down
W: From the woods to the valleys, see how she creeps
W: From the woods to the valleys, see how she creeps
W: Follow, follow the musical horn
W: Sing follow, hark follow, the innocent hare.
W:
W: 4. All along the green turf she pants for breath
W: The huntsman he cries out for death
W: All along the green turf she pants for breath
W: The huntsman he cries out for death
W: Relope, relope, retiring hare
W: Relope, relope, retiring hare
W: Follow, follow the musical horn
W: Sing follow, hark follow, the innocent hare.
W:
W: 5. This hare has led us a noble run
W: Success to sportsman, every one
W: This hare has led us a noble run
W: Success to sportsman, every one
W: Such a chase she has led us, four hours or more
W: Such a chase she has led us, four hours or more
W: Wine and beer we'll drink without fear
W: We'll drink a success to the innocent hare.
