w: sent it un--to Lord Al-len-wa-ter to_ read it if_ he could.
%
W: 2. The first two lines Lord Allenwater read
W: They struck him with surprise,
W: And the next two lines Lord Allenwater read
W: Made tears fall from his eyes.
W:
W: 3. He goes up to his gay lady
W: As she in child bed lay,
W: And says, "To London I must go,
W: I'm sure there is great need."
W:
W: 4. "Well, if to London you must go,
W: Before you go away
W: Make your will, my dear," she said,
W: "Lest you should go astray."
W:
W: 5. "Well, I will leave my only son
W: My houses and my land;
W: And I will leave my dear wedded wife
W: Ten thousand pounds in hand."
W:
W: 6. And he goes out to his stable groom
W: To saddle his milk-white steed;
W: Said, up to London he might ride,
W: "I'm sure there is great need."
W:
W: 7. And he put a foot into the stirrup,
W: The other across his steed;
W: And the gay gold rings from his fingers burst,
W: His nose began to bleed.
W:
W: 8. And as he was riding along the road
W: His horse caught against a stone.
W: "Oh, there's signs and tokens enough I've seen,
W: I'm sure I'll never return."
W:
W: 9. And as he was a-riding up a merry London street
W: So close up the fair Whitehall,
W: Oh, the lords and the ladies stood looking hard,
W: And a traitor he was called.
W:
W: 10. "No traitor at all," Lord Allenwater said,
W: "No traitor at all," cried he,
W: "Why, I vow I can find you three score men
W: To fight for King Georgie."
W:
W: 11. Then it's up and bespoke a grey-headed man,
W: A broad axe in his hand,
W: "Oh deliver your soul, Lord Allenwater,
W: Your life's at my command."
W:
W: 12. "My life I do not value too,
W: My life I will give unto thee,
W: And the black velvet coat that I have on my back,
W: You take that for your fee.
W:
W: 13. There's forty pounds in one pocket,
W: Pray give it unto the poor,
W: And there's forty-five in the other one,
W: Pray give it from door to door."
W:
W: 14. And he laid his head upon the block,
W: The man gave a mighty blow.
W: "Now there lies the head of a traitor," he said,
W: But it answered and it said, "No!"
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_57cb25e3.abc

