W: 1. As I gaed doon by Strichen toon,
W: I heard a fair maid mournin',
W: And she was makin' sair complaint
W: For her true love ne'er returnin'.
W:
W: [Chorus:]
W: Sae fare ye weel, ye Mormond Braes,
W: Where aft-times I've been cheery;
W: Fare ye weel, ye Mormond Braes,
W: For it's there I've lost my deary.
W:
W: 2. There's mony a horse has snappert an' fa'n
W: An' risen again fu' rarely,
W: There's mony a lass has lost her lad
W: An' gotten anither richt early. {Chorus]
W:
W: 3. There's as guid fish intae the sea
W: As ever yet was taken,
W: So I'll cast my net and try again
W: For I'm only aince forsaken. {Chorus]
W:
W: 4. Sae I'll gae doon tae Strichen toon,
W: Whaur I was bred an' born in,
W: An' there I'll get anither sweetheart,
W: Will marry me in the mornin'. {Chorus]
