W: 1. My bonny moorhen, my bonny moorhen,
W: Up in the grey hills, down in the glen;
W: When ye gang butt the house, when ye gang ben,
W: For drink a health to my bonny moorhen.
W:
W: My bonny moorhen's gane over the main
W: And it will be summer when he comes again;
W: But when he comes back again some folk will ken,
W: For joy be with you, my bonny moorhen.
W:
W:
W: 2. My bonny moorhen has feathers anew,
W: They're all fine colours but nane o' them blue.
W: He's red and he's white and he's green and he's grey,
W: My bonny moorhen, come hither away.
W:
W: Come up by Glenouicm and down by Glenmore,
W: Round by Kinclaven and hither tae me;
W: For Ronald and Donald are oot on the fen
W: Tae break the wing of my bonny moorhen.
