W: Chorus:
W:
W: Here's one, two, three jolly lads all in one mind
W: We have come a pace egging and we hope you'll prove kind
W: We hope you'll prove kind with your eggs and strong beer
W: For we'll come no more nigh you until the next year
W:
W: 1. And the first that comes in is Lord Nelson you'll see
W: With a bunch of blue ribbons tied round by his knee
W: And a star on his breast that like silver do shine
W: And I hope he remembers it's pace egging time
W:
W: 2. And the next that comes in, it is Lord Collingwood
W: He fought with Lord Nelson till he shed his blood
W: And he's come from the sea old England to view
W: And he's come a pace egging with all of his crew
W:
W: 3. The next that comes in is our Jolly Jack Tar
W: He sailed with Lord Nelson all through the last war
W: He's arrived from the sea, old England to view
W: And he's come a pace egging with our jovial crew
W:
W: Chorus:
W:
W: Here's one, two, three jolly lads all in one mind
W: We have come a pace egging and we hope you'll prove kind
W: We hope you'll prove kind with your eggs and strong beer
W: For we'll come no more nigh you until the next year
W:
W: 4. The next that comes in is old miser Brownbags
W: For fear of her money she wears her old rags
W: She's gold and she's silver all laid up in store
W: And she's come a pace egging in hopes to get more
W:
W: 5. And the last to come in is old Tosspot, you see
W: He's a valiant old man and in every degree
W: He's a valiant old man and he wears a pigtail
W: And all his delight is a drinking mulled ale
W:
W: 6. If you can drink one glass, then we can drink two
W: Here's a health to Victoria, the same unto you
W: Mind what you're doing and see that all's right
W: If you give naught, we'll take naught, farewell and goodnight.
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_1dc8eb97.abc

