W: 2. Here Phillis is a darling,
W: As she herself gives out,
W: As tight a lass as ever
W: Did use a double clout;
W: She's brisk and gay and cunning,
W: And wants a wedlock yoke,
W: Her mother was before her
W: As good as ever stroke.
W:
W: 3. Young suitors she had many,
W: From squire up to lord,
W: And daily she refus'd them,
W: For virtue was the word;
W: A saint she would be thought,
W: And dissembled all she could,
W: But jolly rakes all knew she was
W: Of playhouse flesh and blood.
W:
W: 4. Her mother when encouraged
W: With warm Geneva dose,
W: Still cry'd "Take care, dear Philly,
W: To keep thy haunches close."
W: This made her stand out stoutly
W: Opposing all that come,
W: And twenty demi-cannon still
W: Were mounted at her bum.
W:
W: 5. The knight and country squire,
W: Were shot with her disdain,
W: The lawyer was outwitted
W: The hardy soldier slain,
W: The bluff tarpolian sailor,
W: In vain cry'd "Hard a-port,"
W: She buffled all the shirks at sea
W: As the country, town and court;
W:
W: 6. The god of love, grown angry
W: That Phillis seemed so shy,
W: Resolv'd her pride to humble,
W: And rout her "pish and fie;"
W: He sent a slow foot tailor,
W: Who knew well how to stitch,
W: And in a little time had found
W: A button for her britch.
W:
W: 7. Yet was it not so close
W: But 'tis known without all doubt,
W: A little human figure
W: Has secretly dropp'd out,
W: And tho' some petty scandal,
W: Pursue this venial fact,
W: Her mother swears and does avow,
W: Her honour is intact.
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_8ea468de.abc

