%leftmargin 1.25in
%
W:1. Remember, O thou man,
W:O thou man, O thou man,
W:Remember O thou man,
W:Thy time is spent.
W:Remember, O thou man,
W:How thou cams't to me then,
W:And I did what I can,
W:Therefore repent.
W:
W:2. Remember Adam's fall,
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:Remember Adam's fall
W:From heaven to hell!
W:Remember Adam's fall,
W:How we were condemned all
W:To hell perpetual,
W:There for to dwell.
W:
W:3. Remember God's goodness,
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:Remember God's goodness,
W:And promise made!
W:Remember God's goodness,
W:How His only Son He sent
W:Our sins for to redress,
W:Be not afraid.
W:
W:4. The angels all did sing,
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:The angels all did sing,
W:On Sion hill
W:The angels all did sing,
W:Praises to our glorious King,
W:And peace to man living,
W:With a good will!'
W:
W:5. The Shepherds amazed was,
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:The Shepherds amazed was,
W:To hear the angels sing,
W:The Shepherds amazed was
W:How it should come to pass
W:That Christ our Messias
W:Should be our King!
W:
W:6. To Bethlehem did they go,
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:The shepherds three;
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:To Bethlehem did they go,
W:To see whether it were so,
W:Whether Christ were borne or no
W:To set man free.
W:
W:7. As the Angels before did say,
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:As the Angels before did say,
W:So it came to pass;
W:As the Angels before did say,
W:They found him wrapt in hay
W:In a manger, where he lay
W:So poor he was.
W:
W:8. In Bethlehem he was born,
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:In Bethlehem he was born,
W:For mankind's sake;
W:In Bethlehem he was born,
W:For us that were forlorn,
W:And therefore took no scorn
W:Our sins to bear.
W:
W:9. In a manger laid he was,
W:O thou Man, O thou Man,
W:In a manger laid he was
W:At this time present.
W:In a manger laid he was,
W:Between an ox and an ass,
W:And all for our trespass,
W:Therefore repent.
W:
W:10. Give thanks to God always,
W:O thou man, O thou man!
W:Give thanks to God always,
W:With heart most joyfully
W:Give thanks to God always,
W:Upon this blessed day,
W:Let all men sing and say:
W:'Holy, holy!'
