W: 1. Farewell my dear, I must be gone
W: And leave you for a while.
W: If I roam away, I'll come back again,
W: Though I go ten thousand miles, my dear,
W: Though I go ten thousand miles.
W:
W: 2. So fair thou art my bonnie lass,
W: So deep in love am I.
W: But I never will prove false to the bonnie lass I love
W: Til the stars fall from the sky, my dear,
W: Til the stars fall from the sky.
W:
W: 3. The sea will never run dry, my dear
W: Nor the rocks melt with the sun.
W: And I never will prove false to the bonnie lass I love
W: Till all these things be done, my dear,
W: Till all these things be done.
W:
W: 4. Oh, can't you see that pretty turtle dove
W: As she flies from vine to vine?
W: And she's mourning for the loss of her love,
W: Just as I shall do for mine, my dear,
W: Just as I shall do for mine.
