W: 2. All bachelors will to this game
W: And marry'd men likewise;
W: Yea, wives and maids and widows
W: Will use it all their lives:
W: And old men that will have a go
W: Altho' their game's but small,
W: Yet these old colts will have a bout
W: At up-tails all.
W:
W: 3. It cannot be unwholesome.
W: Physicians do it use,
W: And if that it were noysome,
W: They would it then refuse:
W: But if it hurt the body,
W: Then sure their skill is small;
W: For why the best of these will play
W: At up-tails all.
W:
W: 4. All ladies love the pastime,
W: And do the pleasure crave,
W: And if it were a base thing,
W: Then it they would not have:
W: But yet the fairest women,
W: Will soonest for it call;
W: There is no one but that will play
W: At up-tails all.
W:
W: 5. And if it were a costly thing,
W: Then beggars could not buy it,
W: And if it were a loathsome thing
W: Then genteels would defy it:
W: But oh, it is a sweet thing,
W: And pleasing unto all;
W: There is no one but that will play
W: At up-tails all.
