W: 2. I was in Talcahuano last year in a whaler.
W: I bought some gold brooches for the girls in the Bay.
W: I bought me a pipe and they called it a meerscum,
W: And it melted like butter on a hot shiny day.
W:
W: Chorus (after each verse):
W: We’ll rant and we’ll roar like true born young whalermen,
W: We’ll rant and we’ll roar on deck or below,
W: Until we see bottom inside the two sinkers,
W: And straight up the channel to Huasco we’ll go.
W:
W: 3. I went to a dance one night in old Tumbez,
W: There was plenty of girls there as fine as you’d wish.
W: There was one pretty maiden a-chewing tobacco,
W: Just like a young kitten a-chewing fresh fish.
W:
W: 4. Here’s a health to the girls of old Talcahuano,
W: A health to the maidens of far-off Maui.
W: And let you be merry, don’t be melancholy;
W: I can’t marry youse all or in chokey I’d be.
