%%leftmargin 1.75in
%%rightmargin 1.75in
%
W: 1. A match was made for me last night
W: But not to one that I love or like.
W: So I'll steal away long before it is light
W: And I'll roam the wild valleys over.
W:
W: 2. So I rose up just before it was day
W: And I heard the lark and the bluebird say
W: That the glory of summer had faded away
W: And my love had gone over the ocean.
W:
W: 3. O, I walked up and I walked down,
W: I wandered through Cork and Dublin town.
W: But an equal to my love, never was found
W: She's the wee lass that left my heart broken.
W:
W: 4. O, courting at lambing-time is my delight,
W: A bottle of brandy here at my side.
W: A bed of green rushes underneath my head
W: And a charming wee lass in my arms.
