W: 1. It's with Kitty I'll go for a ramble far over the mountains wide,
W: Where the blackbird nests in the brambles in the hills where the eagles glide,
W: Or in some lonely valley where the rooks in the evening nest,
W: And mine with their prayers would mingle when the sun sinks in the west.
W:
W: 2. Oh, me darling wee lass of the heather, your voice is sweet to me
W: As the stars all shining together where the mountains touch to the sea,
W: And all of Erin's bright treasures, her beautiful locks, lakes, and rills
W: Cannot equal one smile from my Kathleen, the queen of the heathery hills.
W:
W: 3. And it's give me the roughest of raiment to last out the life of man.
W: Let my beard grow unkempt and unshaven till it reaches a mile and a span.
W: Like the fleece of the great mountain wether my whiskers will tumble on down.
W: If I can't find a wife in the heather, I'll die in the low, low ground.
%
% Source: sources/dmc-lizmilner-com/pages/viewabc.vbhtml_92c59b22.abc

